From cda56ee4b2c535eed4da19761e4eb75e3ba0cc4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miures Manager <contact@miures.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:44:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Translation intelligence: languages as copilot actions
 (research intelligence, Phase 3)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The copilot now translates, and the engine keeps the translations honest.
A request about languages brings the TRANSLATION GUIDE and, in the outline,
every language version's state, the glossary, the routing and the named
questions' elements with their existing translations; the model writes the
translations and returns them as actions; the engine resolves each target
against the survey (Q5, Q5.option:2 or by label, Q5.row:r1, Q5.instruction,
end:complete, block:Brand, button:next, ui:required, meta:title, or the raw
key) and refuses, element by element and by reason, a dropped or changed
{{pipe}}, unbalanced or mismatched HTML, an empty text and a translated
do-not-translate term — the rest is written as machine translation to review.

Engine (packages/engine/src/localizationActions.ts, new): add_language,
remove_language (destructive), set_language_status (refused for ready/live
while anything blocks), set_translations (approved/reviewed entries kept
unless overwriteApproved; glossary misses warned), approve_translations,
confirm_translations, set_language_routing (country map, URL parameter,
embedded field, rules, switcher, fallback; merge by default; the country and
rules steps inserted ahead of browser detection, and said), set_glossary.
Wired into surveyActions (ranked last, and ordered among themselves so the
language exists before its translations whatever order the model listed),
the Changes summary ("Add Deutsch as a language", "Translate 9 elements into
Deutsch", "Approve…", "Confirm N outdated…", "Change the language routing")
and the review's new localization findings. After every proposal the engine
marks translations whose source changed as outdated — text kept and shown —
and warns: "1 translation is now outdated (de) — the source text changed".

Studio: the system prompt names the actions; COPILOT_TRANSLATION_GUIDE and
translationIntent; the outline's languages block; a block named in a request
focuses all of its questions; the turn route recognises translation turns.
Intelligent → Languages (LanguagesTab): per language the completion bar and
counts, outdated and blocking items, Translate the missing / Re-translate the
outdated (requests), Confirm they still fit / Approve / Mark ready
(proposals through Changes), who gets which language, the glossary. The
Changes panel offers "Re-translate them in this proposal" on the outdated
warning, chaining the re-translation onto the same proposal. Everything
writes def.localization — one localization, shared with the Localization
panel and the runtime.

Tests: engine localizationActions.test.ts (5; 70 mutations, 69 caught, the
one survivor behaviourally equivalent; the follow-up found and fixed a real
gate bug — merge: false was dropped, so a routing replacement always merged);
studio copilot.test.ts (+1; 10/10); browser
scripts/translation-copilot-test.mjs (10 checks; 10/10 against the Studio
surfaces). Engine 1419, Studio 221; copilot, ux-copilot, analysis-framework,
localization, intelligent-mode and review-fixes browser suites green.
Docs: docs/TRANSLATION-INTELLIGENCE-2026-10-04.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
